        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.316,
            0.087,
            0.684,
            0.111
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{CH_{3}COOC_{2}H_{5}}\\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{NaOH}}\\mathrm{C_{2}H_{5}OH}+\\mathrm{CH_{3}COONa}",
          "image_source": "images/page_16_equation_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.28,
            0.112,
            0.892,
            0.161
          ],
          "content": "**(ii) Reaction with a base: Like mineral acids, ethanoic acid reacts with a base such as sodium hydroxide to give a salt (sodium ethanoate or commonly called sodium acetate) and water:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.314,
            0.165,
            0.67,
            0.183
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{NaOH}+\\mathrm{CH_{3}COOH}\\rightarrow\\mathrm{CH_{3}COONa}+\\mathrm{H_{2}O}",
          "image_source": "images/page_16_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.184,
            0.892,
            0.218
          ],
          "content": "**How does ethanoic acid react with carbonates and hydrogencarbonates?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.221,
            0.639,
            0.238
          ],
          "content": "**Let us perform an activity to find out.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.243,
            0.272,
            0.264
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 4.9"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.275,
            0.618,
            0.29
          ],
          "content": "n **Set up the apparatus as shown in Chapter 2, Activity 2.5.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.289,
            0.871,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": "**Take a spatula full of sodium carbonate in a test tube and add 2 mL of dilute ethanoic acid.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.318,
            0.316,
            0.333
          ],
          "content": "n **What do you observe?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.333,
            0.824,
            0.349
          ],
          "content": "n **Pass the gas produced through freshly prepared lime-water. What do you observe?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.348,
            0.871,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": "**Can the gas produced by the reaction between ethanoic acid and sodium carbonate be identified by this test?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.376,
            0.82,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": "n **Repeat this Activity with sodium hydrogencarbonate instead of sodium carbonate.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.405,
            0.899,
            0.47
          ],
          "content": "**(iii) Reaction with carbonates and hydrogencarbonates: Ethanoic acid reacts with carbonates and hydrogencarbonates to give rise to a salt, carbon dioxide and water. The salt produced is commonly called sodium acetate.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.315,
            0.472,
            0.76,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": "2CH_{3}COOH + Na_{2}CO_{3} \\rightarrow 2CH_{3}COONa + H_{2}O + CO_{2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_16_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.315,
            0.495,
            0.744,
            0.516
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{CH_{3}COOH + [NaHCO_{3} \\rightarrow CH_{3}COONa + H_{2}O + CO_{2}]}",
          "image_source": "images/page_16_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.53,
            0.736,
            0.559
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Q U E S T I O N S"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.103,
            0.571,
            0.774,
            0.603
          ],
          "content": "**1. How would you distinguish experimentally between an alcohol and a carboxylic acid?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.102,
            0.608,
            0.389,
            0.625
          ],
          "content": "**2. What are oxidising agents?**"
        },
