          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 4.10"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.455,
            0.706,
            0.871,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": "n **Take about 10 mL of water each in two test tubes.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.455,
            0.721,
            0.872,
            0.749
          ],
          "content": "**Add a drop of oil (cooking oil) to both the test tubes and label them as A and B.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.456,
            0.75,
            0.871,
            0.765
          ],
          "content": "n **To test tube B, add a few drops of soap solution.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.456,
            0.765,
            0.872,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": "**Now shake both the test tubes vigourously for the same period of time.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.455,
            0.794,
            0.873,
            0.837
          ],
          "content": "**Can you see the oil and water layers separately in both the test tubes immediately after you stop shaking them?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.455,
            0.837,
            0.873,
            0.882
          ],
          "content": "**Leave the test tubes undisturbed for some time and observe. Does the oil layer separate out? In which test tube does this happen first?**"
        },
